Description: linux joystick: use the real EVIOCGBTNCNT ioctl number when the headers lack it
 Pull request 14758 falls back to "#define EVIOCGBTNCNT 0" when the kernel
 headers it is built against have no EV_BTN. ioctl(fd, 0, ...) always fails,
 so a library built against older headers (every Debian build until the
 kernel headers carry EV_BTN) never used the kernel's EV_BTN and showed 79
 buttons on a kernel that offers 128. Found by running the 128-button fixture on
 an EV_BTN kernel with the library as the pull request has it. The number is the
 one of the posted kernel series (_IOR('E', 0x1c, unsigned int)); if the kernel
 series changes it, this patch changes with it.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 15), written with Claude Sonnet 5.5
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-07
---
--- a/src/joystick/linux/SDL_sysjoystick.c
+++ b/src/joystick/linux/SDL_sysjoystick.c
@@ -61,6 +61,11 @@
 #define EV_BTN 0x06
 #define EVIOCGBTNCNT 0
 #endif
+#if EVIOCGBTNCNT == 0
+// The fallback above is no ioctl number: ioctl(fd, 0, ...) always fails and the kernel's EV_BTN would never be used
+#undef EVIOCGBTNCNT
+#define EVIOCGBTNCNT _IOR('E', 0x1c, unsigned int)
+#endif
 #ifndef BTN_NORTH
 #define BTN_NORTH 0x133
 #endif
